public import TauCeti.AlgebraicTopology.UniversalCover.Circle.HigherHomotopy
import TauCeti.Algebra.MonoidAlgebra.Exactness

/-!
# The Brown model of the circle

The circle has a cell structure with one `0`-cell and one `1`-cell, attached along a loop `ℓ`
which generates its fundamental group. Brown's twisted tensor product construction turns this cell
structure into a semi-free left module over the loop chain algebra `C_*(Ω_b B; R)`, with one
free generator for each cell: the module `C_*(Ω_b B; R) e₀ ⊕ C_*(Ω_b B; R) e₁`, with `e₀` in
dimension `0`, `e₁` in dimension `1`, and differential

`d e₀ = 0`, `d e₁ = (ℓ - 1) e₀`,

where `ℓ` also denotes the `0`-chain of the loop. This is the row-finite twisted module of the
twisting cocycle `TauCeti.loopSubOneCocycle`, with differential `TauCeti.loopSubOneDifferential`.
The coefficient of `e₀` followed by the augmentation of the loop chain algebra is an augmentation
`TauCeti.loopSubOneAugmentation` onto `R`, linear over the augmentation of `C_*(Ω_b B; R)`.

The main result is that this module is a resolution of `R`
(`TauCeti.exists_loopSubOneDifferential_eq_of_loopSubOneAugmentation_eq_zero`): a cycle of
augmentation zero is a boundary. It holds for every space `B` which is aspherical at `b` and
whose fundamental group is infinite cyclic, generated by the class of `ℓ`, for instance the circle
(`TauCeti.exists_loopSubOneDifferential_eq_of_windingNumber_eq_one`). Over an aspherical space the
loop chain algebra is quasi-isomorphic to the group ring `R[π₁(B, b)]`
(`TauCeti.bijective_cohomologyMap_loopChainToGroupAlgebraDGAlgHom`), and there the
statement is that `ℓ - 1` is a non-zero-divisor generating the augmentation ideal: an element of
the group ring fixed by right multiplication by an element of infinite order is zero
(`MonoidAlgebra.eq_zero_of_mul_single_eq_self`), and the differences `g - 1` for a generating
set generate the augmentation ideal
(`TauCeti.MonoidAlgebra.ker_augmentation_eq_span_of_closure_eq_top`).

The twisting is necessary: with the zero cocycle on the same two generators, the generator `e₁`
is a cycle of augmentation zero which is not a boundary
(`TauCeti.not_exists_rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_zero_eq_single_one`), since the unit of the
loop chain algebra is not a boundary. So the zero cocycle does not give a resolution of `R`.

The Brown model maps to the chains on the based path space `P_b B`, the paths from `b` acted on
by the loops at `b` through concatenation in front
(`TauCeti.loopSubOneComparison`): `e₀` goes to the point chain of the constant path, and `e₁` to
the cone along the truncation homotopy of the point chain of `ℓ`, with a sign, whose boundary is
`ℓ - 1` applied to the constant path. This map is linear over the loop chain algebra, commutes
with the differentials and with the augmentations. When `B` is aspherical at `b` and the class of
`ℓ` generates an infinite cyclic fundamental group `π₁(B, b)`, it is moreover a quasi-isomorphism
(`TauCeti.exists_loopSubOneComparison_add_eq`): every relative cycle is a relative boundary. It is
the comparison of a semi-free resolution with the contractible path fibration
`Ω_b B → P_b B → B`, as in Brown's theorem.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.loopSubOneCocycle R ℓ`: the twisting cocycle with `d e₁ = (ℓ - 1) e₀`.
* `TauCeti.loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ`: the differential of its twisted module.
* `TauCeti.loopSubOneAugmentation R`: the augmentation of the twisted module onto `R`.
* `TauCeti.loopSubOneComparison R H ℓ`: the comparison with the chains on the based path space.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.exists_loopSubOneDifferential_eq_of_loopSubOneAugmentation_eq_zero`: for an aspherical
  space with infinite cyclic fundamental group generated by `ℓ`, the twisted module is a
  resolution of the coefficients.
* `TauCeti.exists_loopSubOneDifferential_eq_of_windingNumber_eq_one`: the case of the circle.
* `TauCeti.not_exists_rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_zero_eq_single_one`: the zero cocycle on two
  generators does not give a resolution.
* `TauCeti.cubicalChainModuleDifferential_loopSubOneComparison`,
  `TauCeti.cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_loopSubOneComparison`: the comparison is a chain map
  compatible with the augmentations.
* `TauCeti.exists_loopSubOneComparison_add_eq`: for an aspherical space with infinite cyclic
  fundamental group generated by `ℓ`, the comparison is a quasi-isomorphism.

## References

* E. H. Brown, *Twisted tensor products, I*, Ann. of Math. (2) 69 (1959), 223–246.
* J.-F. Barraud, M. Damian, V. Humilière, A. Oancea, *Morse homology with differential graded
  coefficients*, Progress in Mathematics 360, Birkhäuser, 2025, Chapters 3--4.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Finsupp

open scoped Topology

namespace TauCeti

section Construction

variable {B : Type*} [TopologicalSpace B] {b : B} {R : Type*} [CommRing R]

/-- The attaching element `ℓ - 1` of the Brown cocycle has degree zero. -/
theorem loopPointChain_sub_one_mem (ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    loopPointChain R ℓ - 1 ∈ cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0 :=
  sub_mem (loopPointChain_mem ℓ) (SetLike.one_mem_graded _)

/-- The dimensions of the cells of the circle: the generator `0` is the `0`-cell and the
generator `1` the `1`-cell. -/
def loopSubOneIndex : Fin 2 → ℤ := fun i ↦ i

@[simp]
theorem loopSubOneIndex_zero : loopSubOneIndex 0 = 0 :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem loopSubOneIndex_one : loopSubOneIndex 1 = 1 :=
  (rfl)

variable (R) in
/-- **The Brown cocycle of the circle**: the twisting cocycle over `C_*(Ω_b B; R)` on a generator
`e₀` of dimension `0` and a generator `e₁` of dimension `1`, with rows `d e₀ = 0` and
`d e₁ = (ℓ - 1) e₀`. -/
def loopSubOneCocycle (ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    RowFiniteTwistingCocycle (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (Fin 2) loopSubOneIndex where
  m := ![0, single 0 (loopPointChain R ℓ - 1)]
  mem_graded x y := by
    fin_cases x <;> dsimp only [Fin.zero_eta, Fin.mk_one]
    · simp
    · fin_cases y <;> dsimp only [Fin.zero_eta, Fin.mk_one]
      · simpa using loopPointChain_sub_one_mem ℓ
      · simp
  twisting x := by
    fin_cases x <;> dsimp only [Fin.zero_eta, Fin.mk_one]
    · simp
    · rw [Matrix.cons_val_one, Matrix.cons_val_zero, mapRange.linearMap_apply, mapRange_single,
        cubicalChainDifferential_eq_zero_of_nonneg _ _ le_rfl (loopPointChain_sub_one_mem ℓ),
        single_zero, sum_single_index (by simp)]
      simp

@[simp]
theorem loopSubOneCocycle_m_zero (ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    (loopSubOneCocycle R ℓ).m 0 = 0 :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem loopSubOneCocycle_m_one (ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    (loopSubOneCocycle R ℓ).m 1 = single 0 (loopPointChain R ℓ - 1) :=
  (rfl)

variable (R) in
/-- The total grading of the twisted module `C_*(Ω_b B) e₀ ⊕ C_*(Ω_b B) e₁`, in which `e₀` has
degree `0` and `e₁` degree `-1`. -/
abbrev loopSubOneGrading : ℤ → Submodule R (Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :=
  rowFiniteTotalGrading (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
    (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) loopSubOneIndex

/-- The loop chain algebra acts on the twisted module additively in degrees. The generic instance
`instGradedSMulRowFiniteTotalGrading` is not found by instance search here, because the module
structure of the loop chain algebra over `R` appears in two definitionally equal forms. -/
instance : SetLike.GradedSMul (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
    (loopSubOneGrading (B := B) (b := b) R) :=
  instGradedSMulRowFiniteTotalGrading (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
    (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (ind := loopSubOneIndex)

variable (R) in
/-- The differential of the twisted module `C_*(Ω_b B) e₀ ⊕ C_*(Ω_b B) e₁` of the Brown cocycle of
the circle. -/
abbrev loopSubOneDifferential (ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    (Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) →ₗ[R] Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R :=
  rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
    (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
    (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopSubOneCocycle R ℓ).m

/-- The twisted module of the Brown cocycle is a differential graded left module over the loop
chain algebra. -/
theorem isDGLeftModule_loopSubOneDifferential (ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    IsDGLeftModule (loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R) (loopSubOneGrading (B := B) (b := b) R)
      (loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ) :=
  (loopSubOneCocycle R ℓ).isDGLeftModule_rowFiniteTwistedDifferential
    (loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R)

/-- The differential on the multiples of `e₀` is the differential of the coefficient. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopSubOneDifferential_single_zero (ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b) (a : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ (single 0 a) =
      single 0 (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R a) := by
  simp [rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_single_koszulTwist]

/-- The differential on a homogeneous multiple of `e₁`:
`d (a e₁) = (d a) e₁ + (-1)^|a| (a (ℓ - 1)) e₀`. -/
theorem loopSubOneDifferential_single_one (ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b) {q : ℤ}
    {a : loopChainAlgebra B b R} (ha : a ∈ cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R q) :
    loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ (single 1 a) =
      single 1 (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R a) +
        q.negOnePow • single 0 (a * (loopPointChain R ℓ - 1)) := by
  rw [rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_single _ _ ha, loopSubOneCocycle_m_one, smul_single,
    smul_eq_mul]

variable (R) in
/-- The **augmentation** of the twisted module of the Brown cocycle: the augmentation of the
loop chain algebra applied to the coefficient of `e₀`. -/
def loopSubOneAugmentation : (Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) →ₗ[R] R :=
  (loopChainAugmentation B b R : loopChainAlgebra B b R →ₐ[R] R).toLinearMap ∘ₗ lapply 0

@[simp]
theorem loopSubOneAugmentation_apply (f : Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopSubOneAugmentation R f = loopChainAugmentation B b R (f 0) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The augmentation vanishes on boundaries. -/
theorem loopSubOneAugmentation_differential (ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (f : Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopSubOneAugmentation R (loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ f) = 0 := by
  induction f using Finsupp.induction_linear with
  | zero => simp
  | add f g hf hg => rw [map_add, map_add, hf, hg, add_zero]
  | single x a =>
    fin_cases x <;> dsimp only [Fin.zero_eta, Fin.mk_one]
    · simp
    · simp [rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_single_koszulTwist]

/-- The augmentation is linear over the augmentation of the loop chain algebra. -/
theorem loopSubOneAugmentation_smul (a : loopChainAlgebra B b R)
    (f : Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopSubOneAugmentation R (a • f) =
      loopChainAugmentation B b R a * loopSubOneAugmentation R f := by
  simp

/-- The augmentation is onto. -/
theorem loopSubOneAugmentation_surjective :
    Function.Surjective (loopSubOneAugmentation (B := B) (b := b) R) :=
  fun r ↦ ⟨single 0 (algebraMap R _ r), by simp⟩

/-- The augmentation vanishes in nonzero total degree. -/
theorem loopSubOneAugmentation_eq_zero_of_mem {n : ℤ} (hn : n ≠ 0)
    {f : Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R}
    (hf : f ∈ loopSubOneGrading R n) :
    loopSubOneAugmentation R f = 0 := by
  have h0 := (mem_rowFiniteTotalGrading_iff _ _).mp hf 0
  rw [loopSubOneIndex_zero, add_zero] at h0
  rcases (mem_cubicalChainGrading_iff _ _).1 h0 with h | ⟨k, y, hk, h⟩
  · simp [h]
  · obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_succ_of_ne_zero (by omega : k ≠ 0)
    simp [← h]

/-- The augmentation only sees the component of total degree zero. -/
theorem loopSubOneAugmentation_decompose (f : Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopSubOneAugmentation R f = loopSubOneAugmentation R
      (DirectSum.decompose (loopSubOneGrading R) f 0 : Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) := by
  induction f using DirectSum.Decomposition.inductionOn (loopSubOneGrading R) with
  | zero => simp
  | @homogeneous n f =>
    by_cases hn : n = 0
    · subst hn
      rw [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same _ f.2]
    · rw [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne _ f.2 hn, loopSubOneAugmentation_eq_zero_of_mem hn f.2,
        map_zero]
  | add f g hf hg =>
    rw [map_add, hf, hg, DirectSum.decompose_add, DirectSum.add_apply, Submodule.coe_add,
      map_add]

end Construction

section Resolution

universe u

variable {B : Type u} [TopologicalSpace B] {b : B} {R : Type u} [CommRing R]

/-- The homogeneous case of
`TauCeti.exists_loopSubOneDifferential_eq_of_loopSubOneAugmentation_eq_zero`. -/
private theorem exists_loopSubOneDifferential_eq_of_mem
    (hB : ∀ n : ℕ, Subsingleton (π_ (n + 2) B b)) {ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b}
    (hgen : Subgroup.zpowers (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b ℓ) = ⊤)
    (hinf : ¬IsOfFinOrder (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b ℓ)) {n : ℤ}
    {f : Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R}
    (hfn : f ∈ loopSubOneGrading R n)
    (hf : loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ f = 0) (hε : loopSubOneAugmentation R f = 0) :
    ∃ u, loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ u = f := by
  set d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R
  set φ := loopChainToGroupAlgebra B b R
  set g := MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b ℓ
  set c := loopPointChain R ℓ - 1 with hc
  have hc0 : c ∈ cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0 := loopPointChain_sub_one_mem ℓ
  have hφc : φ c = MonoidAlgebra.single g 1 - 1 := by
    rw [hc, map_sub, map_one, loopChainToGroupAlgebra_loopPointChain]
  have hs : f 1 ∈ cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (n + 1) := by
    simpa using (mem_rowFiniteTotalGrading_iff _ _).mp hfn 1
  have hfeq : f = single 0 (f 0) + single 1 (f 1) := by
    ext i
    fin_cases i <;> simp
  -- The differential of `f`, read off on the two generators.
  have hDf : loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ f =
      single 0 (d (f 0)) + (single 1 (d (f 1)) + (n + 1).negOnePow • single 0 (f 1 * c)) := by
    conv_lhs => rw [hfeq]
    rw [map_add, loopSubOneDifferential_single_zero, loopSubOneDifferential_single_one ℓ hs]
  have hds : d (f 1) = 0 := by
    simpa [hDf] using congrArg (· 1) hf
  have hdr : d (f 0) + (n + 1).negOnePow • (f 1 * c) = 0 := by
    simpa [hDf] using congrArg (· 0) hf
  -- The coefficient of `e₁` is a boundary, since `ℓ - 1` is a non-zero-divisor in the group ring.
  have hφs : φ (f 1) = 0 := by
    have h1 : φ (f 1 * c) = 0 := by
      have := congrArg φ hdr
      rw [map_add, map_zsmul_unit, loopChainToGroupAlgebra_differential, zero_add,
        map_zero] at this
      exact (smul_eq_zero_iff_eq _).mp this
    rw [map_mul, hφc, mul_sub, mul_one, sub_eq_zero] at h1
    exact MonoidAlgebra.eq_zero_of_mul_single_eq_self hinf h1
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ :=
    exists_cubicalChainDifferential_eq_of_loopChainToGroupAlgebra_eq_zero R hB hds hφs
  set u' := (DirectSum.decompose (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) u n :
    loopChainAlgebra B b R)
  have hu'n : u' ∈ cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R n := SetLike.coe_mem _
  have hu' : d u' = f 1 := by
    rw [(loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R).isDGLeftModule.map_decompose, hu,
      DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same _ hs]
  -- Subtracting the boundary of `u' e₁` leaves a multiple `r' e₀` which is a cycle of
  -- augmentation zero.
  set r' := f 0 - n.negOnePow • (u' * c)
  have hDu : loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ (single 1 u') =
      single 1 (f 1) + n.negOnePow • single 0 (u' * c) := by
    rw [loopSubOneDifferential_single_one ℓ hu'n, hu']
  have hf' : f - loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ (single 1 u') = single 0 r' := by
    conv_lhs => rw [hfeq]
    rw [hDu, single_sub, ← smul_single]
    abel
  have hdr' : d r' = 0 := by
    have := congrArg (loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ) hf'
    rw [map_sub, hf, (loopSubOneCocycle R ℓ).differential_sq_zero (loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R),
      sub_zero,
      loopSubOneDifferential_single_zero] at this
    exact (single_eq_zero.mp this.symm)
  have hεr' : loopChainAugmentation B b R r' = 0 := by
    have := congrArg (loopSubOneAugmentation R) hf'
    rw [map_sub, hε, loopSubOneAugmentation_differential, sub_zero,
      loopSubOneAugmentation_apply, single_eq_same] at this
    exact this.symm
  -- In the group ring, `φ r'` lies in the augmentation ideal, generated by `ℓ - 1`.
  have hker : φ r' ∈ RingHom.ker (MonoidAlgebra.augmentation R (FundamentalGroup B b)) := by
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker, augmentation_loopChainToGroupAlgebra, hεr']
  rw [MonoidAlgebra.ker_augmentation_eq_span_of_closure_eq_top R
    (s := {g}) (by rw [← Subgroup.zpowers_eq_closure, hgen]), Set.image_singleton,
    Ideal.mem_span_singleton'] at hker
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hker
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := loopZeroChainToGroupAlgebra_surjective (X := B) (x := b) (R := R) a
  set q := cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0 y
  have hq0 : q ∈ cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0 := by
    simpa using cubicalChainLof_mem (MooreLoopSpace B b) R y
  have hφq : φ q = a := by
    rw [loopChainToGroupAlgebra_lof_zero, hy]
  have hqc0 : q * c ∈ cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0 := by
    simpa using SetLike.mul_mem_graded hq0 hc0
  -- The difference `r' - q (ℓ - 1)` is a boundary of the loop chain algebra.
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := exists_cubicalChainDifferential_eq_of_loopChainToGroupAlgebra_eq_zero R hB
    (z := r' - q * c)
    (by rw [map_sub, hdr', cubicalChainDifferential_eq_zero_of_nonneg _ _ le_rfl hqc0, sub_zero])
    (by rw [map_sub, map_mul, hφq, hφc, ha, sub_self])
  have hDq : loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ (single 1 q) = single 0 (q * c) := by
    rw [loopSubOneDifferential_single_one ℓ hq0,
      cubicalChainDifferential_eq_zero_of_nonneg _ _ le_rfl hq0, single_zero, zero_add,
      Int.negOnePow_zero, one_smul]
  refine ⟨single 0 w + single 1 q + single 1 u', ?_⟩
  rw [map_add, map_add, loopSubOneDifferential_single_zero, hw, hDq, ← single_add, sub_add_cancel,
    ← hf', sub_add_cancel]

/-- **The Brown model of the circle is a resolution.** Let `B` be aspherical at `b`, and let the
class of the Moore loop `ℓ` generate the fundamental group `π₁(B, b)` and have infinite order, so
that the path component of `b` is a `K(ℤ, 1)` with `π₁` generated by `ℓ`. Then in the twisted module
`C_*(Ω_b B) e₀ ⊕ C_*(Ω_b B) e₁` with `d e₁ = (ℓ - 1) e₀`, every cycle of augmentation zero is a
boundary. Together with `loopSubOneAugmentation_differential` and
`loopSubOneAugmentation_surjective`, this says that the augmentation is a quasi-isomorphism onto
the coefficients. -/
theorem exists_loopSubOneDifferential_eq_of_loopSubOneAugmentation_eq_zero
    (hB : ∀ n : ℕ, Subsingleton (π_ (n + 2) B b)) {ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b}
    (hgen : Subgroup.zpowers (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b ℓ) = ⊤)
    (hinf : ¬IsOfFinOrder (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b ℓ))
    {f : Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R}
    (hf : loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ f = 0) (hε : loopSubOneAugmentation R f = 0) :
    ∃ u, loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ u = f := by
  classical
  set 𝒦 := loopSubOneGrading (B := B) (b := b) R
  have hK := isDGLeftModule_loopSubOneDifferential (B := B) (b := b) (R := R) ℓ
  -- Every homogeneous component is a cycle of augmentation zero, hence a boundary.
  have hcomp (n : ℤ) : (DirectSum.decompose 𝒦 f n : Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) ∈
      LinearMap.range (loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ) := by
    refine exists_loopSubOneDifferential_eq_of_mem hB hgen hinf (SetLike.coe_mem _)
      (hK.map_decompose_eq_zero hf n) ?_
    by_cases hn : n = 0
    · subst hn
      rw [← loopSubOneAugmentation_decompose, hε]
    · exact loopSubOneAugmentation_eq_zero_of_mem hn (SetLike.coe_mem _)
  rw [← DirectSum.sum_support_decompose 𝒦 f]
  exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun n _ ↦ hcomp n

/-- **The Brown model of the circle is a resolution**: for a Moore loop `ℓ` of winding number one
in a real circle, the twisted module `C_*(Ω S¹) e₀ ⊕ C_*(Ω S¹) e₁` with `d e₁ = (ℓ - 1) e₀` has
no cycles of augmentation zero other than boundaries. -/
theorem exists_loopSubOneDifferential_eq_of_windingNumber_eq_one {p : ℝ} [Fact (0 < p)]
    {x : AddCircle p} {R : Type} [CommRing R] {ℓ : MooreLoopSpace (AddCircle p) x}
    (hℓ : AddCircle.windingNumber (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom x ℓ) = 1)
    {f : Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra (AddCircle p) x R}
    (hf : loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ f = 0) (hε : loopSubOneAugmentation R f = 0) :
    ∃ u, loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ u = f := by
  set e := AddCircle.windingNumberIso x
  have hg : e (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom x ℓ) = Multiplicative.ofAdd 1 := hℓ
  refine exists_loopSubOneDifferential_eq_of_loopSubOneAugmentation_eq_zero
    (fun n ↦ inferInstance) ?_ ?_ hf hε
  · rw [eq_top_iff]
    intro y _
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ : ∃ k : ℤ, Multiplicative.ofAdd k = e y := ⟨(e y).toAdd, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨k, e.injective ?_⟩
    rw [map_zpow, hg, ← hk, ← ofAdd_zsmul, smul_eq_mul, mul_one]
  · rw [← orderOf_eq_zero_iff, ← MulEquiv.orderOf_eq e, hg, orderOf_eq_zero_iff,
      isOfFinOrder_ofAdd_iff, isOfFinAddOrder_iff_nsmul_eq_zero]
    rintro ⟨n, hn, h⟩
    simp only [nsmul_eq_mul, mul_one, Nat.cast_eq_zero] at h
    omega

end Resolution

section Zero

variable {B : Type*} [TopologicalSpace B] {b : B} {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [Nontrivial R]

/-- **The zero cocycle on two generators is not a resolution.** In the module
`C_*(Ω_b B) e₀ ⊕ C_*(Ω_b B) e₁` with zero twisting, the generator `e₁`, a cycle of augmentation
zero, is not a boundary. So this module is not a resolution of `R`. -/
theorem not_exists_rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_zero_eq_single_one :
    ¬∃ u : Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R,
      rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
        (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (0 : RowFiniteTwistingCocycle (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
          (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
          (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (Fin 2) loopSubOneIndex).m u =
        single 1 1 := by
  rintro ⟨u, hu⟩
  have h := congrArg (fun v ↦ loopChainAugmentation B b R (v 1)) hu
  simp at h

end Zero

section Comparison

variable {B : Type*} [TopologicalSpace B] {b : B} (R : Type*) [CommRing R] (H : Type*)

/-- **The comparison of the Brown model of the circle with the chains on the based path space.**
The loop-chain-linear map `C_*(Ω_b B) e₀ ⊕ C_*(Ω_b B) e₁ → C_*(P_b B)` sending `e₀` to the point
chain `[b]` of the constant path and `e₁` to `-K(ℓ · [b])`, where `K` is the cone along the
truncation homotopy of `P_b B`. -/
def loopSubOneComparison (ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    (Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) →ₗ[loopChainAlgebra B b R]
      cubicalChainModule (MoorePathFrom B b) H R :=
  linearCombination _ ![reflPathChain H R,
    -cubicalChainModuleCone R MoorePathFrom.truncateHomotopy
      (loopPointChain R ℓ • reflPathChain H R)]

variable {R H}

@[simp]
theorem loopSubOneComparison_single_zero (ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b) (a : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopSubOneComparison R H ℓ (single 0 a) = a • reflPathChain H R := by
  simp [loopSubOneComparison]

@[simp]
theorem loopSubOneComparison_single_one (ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b) (a : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopSubOneComparison R H ℓ (single 1 a) =
      a • -cubicalChainModuleCone R MoorePathFrom.truncateHomotopy
        (loopPointChain R ℓ • reflPathChain H R) := by
  simp [loopSubOneComparison]

/-- The image of `e₁` has boundary `(ℓ - 1) · [b]`. -/
private theorem cubicalChainModuleDifferential_neg_cone (ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom B b) H R
        (-cubicalChainModuleCone R MoorePathFrom.truncateHomotopy
          (loopPointChain R ℓ • reflPathChain H R)) =
      (loopPointChain R ℓ - 1) • reflPathChain H R := by
  have hM := pathFromChain_isDGLeftModule B b H R
  have hd : cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom B b) H R
      (loopPointChain R ℓ • reflPathChain H R) = 0 :=
    hM.map_smul_eq_zero_of_map_eq_zero (cubicalChainDifferential_loopPointChain ℓ)
      cubicalChainModuleDifferential_reflPathChain
  have key := cubicalChainModuleDifferential_cone_add_cone_differential
    (G := H) (R := R) (MoorePathFrom.truncateHomotopy (X := B) (b := b))
    (loopPointChain R ℓ • reflPathChain H R)
  rw [hd, map_zero, add_zero, pathFromChainAugmentation_smul,
    loopChainAugmentation_loopPointChain, one_mul, cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_reflPathChain,
    one_smul] at key
  rw [map_neg, key, ← reflPathChain_def, neg_sub, sub_smul, one_smul]

/-- **The comparison is a chain map.** -/
theorem cubicalChainModuleDifferential_loopSubOneComparison (ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (f : Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom B b) H R (loopSubOneComparison R H ℓ f) =
      loopSubOneComparison R H ℓ (loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ f) := by
  refine (linearCombination_rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (pathFromChain_isDGLeftModule B b H R)
    _ (fun x ↦ ?_) f).symm
  fin_cases x <;> dsimp only [Fin.zero_eta, Fin.mk_one]
  · simp
  · rw [loopSubOneCocycle_m_one, linearCombination_single, Matrix.cons_val_zero,
      Matrix.cons_val_one, Matrix.cons_val_zero, cubicalChainModuleDifferential_neg_cone]

/-- **The comparison is compatible with the augmentations.** -/
@[simp]
theorem cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_loopSubOneComparison (ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (f : Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    cubicalChainModuleAugmentation (MoorePathFrom B b) H R (loopSubOneComparison R H ℓ f) =
      loopSubOneAugmentation R f := by
  induction f using Finsupp.induction_linear with
  | zero => simp
  | add f g hf hg => rw [map_add, map_add, hf, hg, map_add]
  | single x a =>
    fin_cases x <;> dsimp only [Fin.zero_eta, Fin.mk_one]
    · simp [pathFromChainAugmentation_smul]
    · rw [loopSubOneComparison_single_one, pathFromChainAugmentation_smul, map_neg,
        cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_cone]
      simp

end Comparison

section ComparisonQuasiIso

universe u

variable {B : Type u} [TopologicalSpace B] {b : B} {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {H : Type*}

/-- **The comparison is a quasi-isomorphism.** Under the hypotheses of
`exists_loopSubOneDifferential_eq_of_loopSubOneAugmentation_eq_zero`, every relative cycle of the
comparison `C_*(Ω_b B) e₀ ⊕ C_*(Ω_b B) e₁ → C_*(P_b B)` is a relative boundary: if `d z = 0` and
the image of `z` is the boundary of `w`, then `z = d u` and `w` is the image of `u` up to a
boundary. Both sides are resolutions of the coefficients, compatibly with the augmentations. -/
theorem exists_loopSubOneComparison_add_eq (hB : ∀ n : ℕ, Subsingleton (π_ (n + 2) B b))
    {ℓ : MooreLoopSpace B b}
    (hgen : Subgroup.zpowers (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b ℓ) = ⊤)
    (hinf : ¬IsOfFinOrder (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b ℓ))
    {z : Fin 2 →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R} {w : cubicalChainModule (MoorePathFrom B b) H R}
    (hz : loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ z = 0)
    (hzw : loopSubOneComparison R H ℓ z =
      cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom B b) H R w) :
    ∃ u v, loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ u = z ∧
      loopSubOneComparison R H ℓ u + cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom B b) H R v =
        w := by
  have hεz : loopSubOneAugmentation R z = 0 := by
    rw [← cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_loopSubOneComparison (H := H) ℓ, hzw,
      cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_differential]
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := exists_loopSubOneDifferential_eq_of_loopSubOneAugmentation_eq_zero hB hgen
    hinf hz hεz
  -- Correct `u` by a multiple of the cycle `e₀` so that `w - c u` has augmentation zero.
  set u' := u + single 0 (algebraMap R _
    (cubicalChainModuleAugmentation (MoorePathFrom B b) H R w - loopSubOneAugmentation R u))
  have hu' : loopSubOneDifferential R ℓ u' = z := by
    rw [map_add, hu, loopSubOneDifferential_single_zero,
      (loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R).map_algebraMap, single_zero, add_zero]
  have hcyc : cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom B b) H R
      (w - loopSubOneComparison R H ℓ u') = 0 := by
    rw [map_sub, cubicalChainModuleDifferential_loopSubOneComparison, hu', hzw, sub_self]
  have hεw : cubicalChainModuleAugmentation (MoorePathFrom B b) H R
      (w - loopSubOneComparison R H ℓ u') = 0 := by
    simp [u']
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := exists_pathFromChainDifferential_eq_of_augmentation_eq_zero hcyc hεw
  exact ⟨u', v, hu', by rw [hv, add_sub_cancel]⟩

end ComparisonQuasiIso

end TauCeti
